<BaseLayout title="About Tolvira" description="Learn why Tolvira is building a global collection of fast, free and privacy-conscious online tools.">
  <header class="page-head"><div class="narrow"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>Small tools, thoughtfully made</h1><p class="lede">Tolvira is an open collection of focused online utilities designed to solve everyday tasks without accounts, clutter or unnecessary data collection.</p></div></header>
  <article class="section narrow prose"><h2>What we are building</h2><p>Each Tolvira tool is a small, independent web application. The central hub helps people discover them, while each tool can evolve, deploy and fail independently.</p><h2>How tools should work</h2><p>Whenever practical, processing happens locally in your browser. Every tool must describe its real behavior; local processing is never claimed when a remote service receives your data.</p><h2>Our principles</h2><ul><li>Useful before decorative.</li><li>Accessible by keyboard and across screen sizes.</li><li>Fast on real devices and networks.</li><li>Transparent about availability, limitations and privacy.</li><li>Free to use without mandatory registration.</li></ul><h2>Current status</h2><p>The hub foundation and tool roadmap are public. Tools become clickable only after their independent applications are implemented and published.</p></article>
</BaseLayout>
